<title>USA: US Stockpile gets bids for surplus aluminum oxide.</title>
<headline>US Stockpile gets bids for surplus aluminum oxide.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three firms bid on Tuesday to buy surplus U.S. aluminum oxide, abrasive grain, with bids ranging from $475 to $480 per short ton, the Defense National Stockpile Center said.</p>
<p>Sunbelt Industries of Voorheesville, New York, was the high bidder, bidding $480 per short ton for a total of 44 short tons.</p>
